1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,820
This is a full SAT math module.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:08,529
Twenty-two original questions,
built to mirror the real thing:

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,260
the same four content domains, the
same mix of multiple choice and

4
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:18,490
student-produced response, and questions
that go from easiest to hardest.

5
00:00:18,946 --> 00:00:24,606
On the real digital SAT, each math
module gives you thirty-five minutes for

6
00:00:24,626 --> 00:00:25,886
twenty-two questions.

7
00:00:25,906 --> 00:00:29,636
That works out to about
ninety-five seconds per question.

8
00:00:29,746 --> 00:00:33,046
The Desmos calculator is
allowed on every question,

9
00:00:33,066 --> 00:00:34,755
so use it here too.

10
00:00:35,216 --> 00:00:36,306
Here's the plan.

11
00:00:36,696 --> 00:00:40,586
In a moment, I'll scroll through
all twenty-two questions.

12
00:00:40,616 --> 00:00:43,755
Pause on each screen and
copy the question down,

13
00:00:43,775 --> 00:00:45,146
or take a screenshot.

14
00:00:45,615 --> 00:00:50,226
Then set a thirty-five minute timer and
take the whole module in one sitting.

15
00:00:50,766 --> 00:00:55,096
When you're done, press play, and we'll
go through every question in order.

16
00:00:55,206 --> 00:00:59,415
Before each solution, there's a short
pause in case you want one more look.

17
00:00:59,486 --> 00:01:04,095
At the end, you'll score yourself by
domain and see exactly what to review.

18
00:01:04,563 --> 00:01:06,063
One note before we start.

19
00:01:06,083 --> 00:01:09,543
Every question here was
written for this video,

20
00:01:09,563 --> 00:01:12,053
in the style of the SAT.

21
00:01:12,163 --> 00:01:15,693
None of them are official
College Board questions.

22
00:01:16,105 --> 00:01:17,525
Here's the full module.

23
00:01:17,545 --> 00:01:19,685
Questions one through seven come first.

24
00:01:19,705 --> 00:01:23,725
These are the warm-up questions, so try
to move through them quickly and bank

25
00:01:23,745 --> 00:01:25,115
some time for the end.

26
00:01:34,606 --> 00:01:36,346
Questions eight through fifteen.

27
00:01:36,366 --> 00:01:40,306
This is the middle of the
module: a word problem system,

28
00:01:40,326 --> 00:01:44,745
a probability table, quadratics,
an exponential model,

29
00:01:44,765 --> 00:01:46,346
and a right triangle.

30
00:01:46,366 --> 00:01:48,776
Most of your time should go here.

31
00:01:59,215 --> 00:02:00,795
Questions sixteen through twenty-two.

32
00:02:00,815 --> 00:02:03,675
These are the hardest ones in the set.

33
00:02:03,695 --> 00:02:06,835
If one stalls you, flag it, make a guess,

34
00:02:06,855 --> 00:02:09,305
move on, and come back if you have time.

35
00:02:19,735 --> 00:02:21,155
Last thing.

36
00:02:21,175 --> 00:02:24,305
Six of these questions
have no answer choices.

37
00:02:24,455 --> 00:02:29,304
For those, you type your answer,
and a fraction or a decimal is fine.

38
00:02:29,374 --> 00:02:32,034
Now pause the video, start your timer,

39
00:02:32,054 --> 00:02:33,054
and go.

40
00:02:33,349 --> 00:02:34,009
Welcome back.

41
00:02:34,029 --> 00:02:35,049
Let's check your work.

42
00:02:35,069 --> 00:02:36,449
Question one.

43
00:02:36,469 --> 00:02:41,169
If three times the quantity
x minus two equals eighteen,

44
00:02:41,189 --> 00:02:43,319
what is the value of x?

45
00:02:43,849 --> 00:02:45,139
Pause and try it.

46
00:02:50,999 --> 00:02:55,369
The cleanest move is to divide
both sides by three first.

47
00:02:55,399 --> 00:02:58,969
That leaves x minus two equals six.

48
00:02:59,199 --> 00:03:03,289
Add two to both sides, and x equals eight.

49
00:03:03,519 --> 00:03:05,568
The answer is D.

50
00:03:06,022 --> 00:03:08,912
The wrong answers come from small slips.

51
00:03:08,941 --> 00:03:12,202
Six is where you stop
after dividing by three.

52
00:03:12,222 --> 00:03:16,481
Four is what you get if you
subtract two instead of adding it.

53
00:03:16,501 --> 00:03:21,392
And twenty thirds comes from multiplying
the three by x but not by the two.

54
00:03:21,864 --> 00:03:23,274
Question two.

55
00:03:23,384 --> 00:03:26,834
A store sells a backpack
for forty-eight dollars.

56
00:03:26,984 --> 00:03:30,834
During a sale, the price is
reduced by twenty-five percent.

57
00:03:30,943 --> 00:03:33,124
What is the sale price of the backpack,

58
00:03:33,144 --> 00:03:34,273
in dollars?

59
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:36,010
Pause and try it.

60
00:03:41,870 --> 00:03:46,770
A twenty-five percent decrease means you
keep seventy-five percent of the price.

61
00:03:46,790 --> 00:03:50,610
So multiply forty-eight
by zero point seven five.

62
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:52,160
That's thirty-six.

63
00:03:52,349 --> 00:03:54,160
The answer is C.

64
00:03:54,607 --> 00:03:57,627
Twelve is the discount,
not the sale price.

65
00:03:57,647 --> 00:04:01,667
Twenty-three is what you get if you
subtract twenty-five dollars instead of

66
00:04:01,687 --> 00:04:02,947
twenty-five percent.

67
00:04:02,967 --> 00:04:06,066
And sixty is a twenty-five
percent increase.

68
00:04:06,086 --> 00:04:09,016
Always check which number
the question wants:

69
00:04:09,086 --> 00:04:11,177
the discount, or what's left.

70
00:04:11,644 --> 00:04:13,024
Question three.

71
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:18,704
Which expression is equivalent
to the quantity two x plus three,

72
00:04:18,724 --> 00:04:21,774
times the quantity x minus four?

73
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:23,470
Pause and try it.

74
00:04:29,330 --> 00:04:33,940
Multiply every term in the first
group by every term in the second.

75
00:04:33,970 --> 00:04:37,190
Two x times x is two x squared.

76
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:40,709
Two x times negative
four is negative eight x.

77
00:04:40,729 --> 00:04:42,990
Three times x is three x.

78
00:04:43,010 --> 00:04:46,260
And three times negative
four is negative twelve.

79
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:48,390
Combine the middle terms.

80
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:52,720
Negative eight x plus
three x is negative five x.

81
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:58,200
So the expression is two x
squared minus five x minus twelve.

82
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:00,150
The answer is B.

83
00:05:00,632 --> 00:05:03,851
Choice A skips the middle terms entirely.

84
00:05:03,871 --> 00:05:09,402
C and D come from sign mistakes with
the negative eight x and the three x.

85
00:05:09,672 --> 00:05:13,961
If you want a check, graph the
original and your choice in Desmos.

86
00:05:14,432 --> 00:05:17,962
Equivalent expressions
draw the exact same curve.

87
00:05:18,423 --> 00:05:19,873
Question four.

88
00:05:20,223 --> 00:05:25,883
A plumber uses the equation C equals
sixty-five h plus ninety to find the total

89
00:05:25,903 --> 00:05:30,832
charge C, in dollars, for
a job that takes h hours.

90
00:05:30,943 --> 00:05:35,513
What is the best interpretation
of ninety in this context?

91
00:05:35,927 --> 00:05:37,217
Pause and try it.

92
00:05:43,077 --> 00:05:48,047
In a linear model, the number
multiplied by the variable is the rate,

93
00:05:48,237 --> 00:05:51,806
and the number standing
alone is the starting value.

94
00:05:51,917 --> 00:05:56,536
Sixty-five is attached to h,
so it's the charge per hour.

95
00:05:56,556 --> 00:05:59,167
Ninety isn't attached to anything.

96
00:05:59,558 --> 00:06:02,207
Quick test: plug in zero hours.

97
00:06:02,277 --> 00:06:03,898
C equals ninety.

98
00:06:03,918 --> 00:06:06,938
So ninety gets charged no
matter how long the job takes.

99
00:06:06,958 --> 00:06:09,017
It's the fixed fee for each job.

100
00:06:09,037 --> 00:06:10,688
The answer is A.

101
00:06:11,095 --> 00:06:12,825
C is the trap.

102
00:06:13,015 --> 00:06:16,835
A one hour job would cost
sixty-five plus ninety,

103
00:06:16,855 --> 00:06:18,835
which is one hundred fifty-five dollars,

104
00:06:18,855 --> 00:06:19,995
not ninety.

105
00:06:20,015 --> 00:06:24,035
And D can't work, because
C is measured in dollars,

106
00:06:24,055 --> 00:06:26,105
so ninety is a dollar amount.

107
00:06:26,556 --> 00:06:27,936
Question five.

108
00:06:27,956 --> 00:06:33,416
In triangle A B C, the measure of
angle A is forty-eight degrees,

109
00:06:33,436 --> 00:06:38,125
and the measure of angle B is
twice the measure of angle C.

110
00:06:38,635 --> 00:06:42,166
What is the measure,
in degrees, of angle C?

111
00:06:42,666 --> 00:06:43,956
Pause and try it.

112
00:06:49,816 --> 00:06:53,115
The angles in a triangle add up
to one hundred eighty degrees.

113
00:06:53,135 --> 00:06:54,556
That's on the reference sheet.

114
00:06:54,576 --> 00:06:56,676
Call angle C x.

115
00:06:56,696 --> 00:06:59,076
Then angle B is two x.

116
00:06:59,096 --> 00:07:04,225
So forty-eight plus two x plus
x equals one hundred eighty.

117
00:07:04,657 --> 00:07:08,146
That's three x plus forty-eight
equals one hundred eighty.

118
00:07:08,257 --> 00:07:12,307
Subtract forty-eight, and three
x equals one hundred thirty-two.

119
00:07:12,577 --> 00:07:15,587
Divide by three, and x is forty-four.

120
00:07:15,656 --> 00:07:17,066
Type forty-four.

121
00:07:17,633 --> 00:07:19,852
Before you move on, reread the question.

122
00:07:19,872 --> 00:07:22,923
It asks for angle C, not angle B.

123
00:07:22,993 --> 00:07:24,933
Angle B would be eighty-eight.

124
00:07:24,953 --> 00:07:30,333
And the three angles check out: forty-eight
plus eighty-eight plus forty-four is

125
00:07:30,353 --> 00:07:31,763
one hundred eighty.

126
00:07:32,212 --> 00:07:33,622
Question six.

127
00:07:33,892 --> 00:07:41,021
The function f is defined by f of
x equals x squared minus three x.

128
00:07:41,211 --> 00:07:44,582
What is the value of f of negative two?

129
00:07:45,042 --> 00:07:46,332
Pause and try it.

130
00:07:52,192 --> 00:07:55,681
Replace every x with
negative two, in parentheses.

131
00:07:55,712 --> 00:07:58,652
Negative two, squared, is positive four.

132
00:07:58,672 --> 00:08:02,331
Negative three times
negative two is positive six.

133
00:08:02,351 --> 00:08:04,372
Four plus six is ten.

134
00:08:04,392 --> 00:08:06,042
The answer is D.

135
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:08,786
Every wrong answer here is a sign error.

136
00:08:08,806 --> 00:08:11,947
If you squared negative
two and got negative four,

137
00:08:11,967 --> 00:08:13,467
you'd land on two.

138
00:08:13,487 --> 00:08:17,467
If you turned negative three times
negative two into negative six,

139
00:08:17,487 --> 00:08:19,066
you'd get negative two.

140
00:08:19,086 --> 00:08:22,016
Make both mistakes, and
you get negative ten.

141
00:08:22,444 --> 00:08:26,254
If negatives make you nervous,
Desmos is a safe check.

142
00:08:26,444 --> 00:08:31,853
Type f of x equals x squared
minus three x on one line.

143
00:08:31,964 --> 00:08:35,814
Then type f of negative
two on the next line.

144
00:08:35,884 --> 00:08:37,773
Desmos shows ten.

145
00:08:38,197 --> 00:08:39,447
Question seven.

146
00:08:39,557 --> 00:08:43,017
A line in the x y plane
passes through the points two,

147
00:08:43,037 --> 00:08:45,457
five, and six, seventeen.

148
00:08:45,477 --> 00:08:49,606
What is the y coordinate of
the y intercept of the line?

149
00:08:50,072 --> 00:08:51,362
Pause and try it.

150
00:08:57,222 --> 00:09:01,442
Start with the slope: change
in y over change in x.

151
00:09:01,462 --> 00:09:04,362
Seventeen minus five is twelve.

152
00:09:04,382 --> 00:09:06,482
Six minus two is four.

153
00:09:06,502 --> 00:09:08,752
Twelve over four is three.

154
00:09:09,159 --> 00:09:13,369
Now plug one point into
y equals three x plus b.

155
00:09:13,559 --> 00:09:19,488
Using two, five: five equals six plus b.

156
00:09:19,519 --> 00:09:21,778
So b is negative one.

157
00:09:21,798 --> 00:09:25,339
The line is y equals three x minus one,

158
00:09:25,359 --> 00:09:27,369
and the answer is negative one.

159
00:09:27,815 --> 00:09:30,395
Negative answers are
allowed in the answer box.

160
00:09:30,415 --> 00:09:32,515
Just type the negative sign first.

161
00:09:32,535 --> 00:09:35,475
And check with the other
point: three times six,

162
00:09:35,495 --> 00:09:37,825
minus one, is seventeen.

163
00:09:37,894 --> 00:09:38,985
It works.

164
00:09:39,515 --> 00:09:42,254
Quick pacing check before question eight.

165
00:09:42,274 --> 00:09:46,775
Seven questions at ninety-five
seconds each is about eleven minutes.

166
00:09:46,795 --> 00:09:50,134
If the first seven took
you a lot longer than that,

167
00:09:50,154 --> 00:09:53,574
the time came out of the
hard questions at the end,

168
00:09:53,594 --> 00:09:55,205
which need it most.

169
00:09:55,658 --> 00:09:56,908
Question eight.

170
00:09:57,138 --> 00:10:00,398
A theater sold two hundred
twenty tickets for a play.

171
00:10:00,418 --> 00:10:02,798
Adult tickets cost twelve dollars each,

172
00:10:02,818 --> 00:10:05,398
and student tickets
cost seven dollars each.

173
00:10:05,418 --> 00:10:10,037
The theater collected a total of two
thousand one hundred forty dollars from

174
00:10:10,057 --> 00:10:11,037
ticket sales.

175
00:10:11,057 --> 00:10:14,148
How many adult tickets
did the theater sell?

176
00:10:14,602 --> 00:10:15,892
Pause and try it.

177
00:10:21,752 --> 00:10:23,572
Two unknowns, so two equations.

178
00:10:23,592 --> 00:10:27,732
Let a be adult tickets
and s be student tickets.

179
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:32,401
The ticket count gives a plus
s equals two hundred twenty.

180
00:10:32,592 --> 00:10:38,922
The money gives twelve a plus seven s
equals two thousand one hundred forty.

181
00:10:39,452 --> 00:10:40,452
Substitute.

182
00:10:40,692 --> 00:10:45,182
From the first equation, s equals
two hundred twenty minus a.

183
00:10:45,212 --> 00:10:52,591
So twelve a plus seven times the quantity
two hundred twenty minus a equals two

184
00:10:52,611 --> 00:10:54,472
thousand one hundred forty.

185
00:10:54,492 --> 00:10:59,912
That simplifies to five a plus one
thousand five hundred forty equals two

186
00:10:59,932 --> 00:11:02,022
thousand one hundred forty.

187
00:11:02,435 --> 00:11:05,535
Subtract one thousand five hundred forty,

188
00:11:05,555 --> 00:11:07,855
and five a equals six hundred.

189
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:10,445
So a equals one hundred twenty.

190
00:11:10,554 --> 00:11:12,324
The answer is C.

191
00:11:12,434 --> 00:11:15,734
One hundred is the number
of student tickets.

192
00:11:15,754 --> 00:11:18,765
That's the trap if you solved
for the wrong variable.

193
00:11:19,231 --> 00:11:21,411
Desmos does this in seconds.

194
00:11:21,431 --> 00:11:25,051
Use x for adult tickets
and y for student tickets.

195
00:11:25,071 --> 00:11:28,571
Type x plus y equals two hundred twenty,

196
00:11:28,591 --> 00:11:34,051
and twelve x plus seven y equals
two thousand one hundred forty.

197
00:11:34,071 --> 00:11:36,331
Zoom out, click where the lines cross,

198
00:11:36,351 --> 00:11:39,401
and you get one hundred
twenty, one hundred.

199
00:11:39,854 --> 00:11:41,154
Question nine.

200
00:11:41,174 --> 00:11:46,274
The table shows the results of a survey
in which two hundred students chose

201
00:11:46,294 --> 00:11:48,833
their favorite sport to watch.

202
00:11:48,853 --> 00:11:55,064
Of the tenth graders, forty-five chose
soccer and thirty-five chose basketball.

203
00:11:55,134 --> 00:12:00,344
Of the eleventh graders, seventy chose
soccer and fifty chose basketball.

204
00:12:00,778 --> 00:12:05,478
If one of the students who chose
basketball is selected at random,

205
00:12:05,498 --> 00:12:09,468
what is the probability that the
student is in eleventh grade?

206
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:11,210
Pause and try it.

207
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:21,520
The key phrase is, one of the
students who chose basketball.

208
00:12:21,830 --> 00:12:24,010
That shrinks the group
you're choosing from.

209
00:12:24,030 --> 00:12:27,209
You're not choosing from all
two hundred students anymore.

210
00:12:27,229 --> 00:12:30,440
You're only choosing from
the basketball column.

211
00:12:30,989 --> 00:12:34,478
That column has eighty-five
students in total.

212
00:12:34,949 --> 00:12:37,289
Fifty of them are in eleventh grade.

213
00:12:37,309 --> 00:12:40,769
So the probability is
fifty over eighty-five,

214
00:12:40,789 --> 00:12:44,039
which simplifies to ten seventeenths.

215
00:12:44,109 --> 00:12:46,119
The answer is C.

216
00:12:46,590 --> 00:12:50,880
Each wrong answer uses the wrong
denominator or the wrong column.

217
00:12:51,750 --> 00:12:56,120
One fourth is fifty over
all two hundred students.

218
00:12:56,229 --> 00:13:00,010
Five twelfths is fifty over
all the eleventh graders.

219
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:04,410
And fourteen twenty-thirds is
seventy over one hundred fifteen,

220
00:13:04,430 --> 00:13:05,800
from the soccer column.

221
00:13:06,338 --> 00:13:09,548
Watch for the different
ways the SAT can say this.

222
00:13:09,778 --> 00:13:12,678
Given that the student chose basketball.

223
00:13:12,698 --> 00:13:16,548
Of the students who chose basketball.

224
00:13:17,298 --> 00:13:19,428
A student who chose basketball.

225
00:13:19,618 --> 00:13:23,708
Each one tells you the same thing:
that group is your denominator.

226
00:13:24,136 --> 00:13:25,076
Question ten.

227
00:13:25,096 --> 00:13:30,316
What is the sum of the solutions to the
equation two x squared minus seven x

228
00:13:30,336 --> 00:13:32,746
minus fifteen equals zero?

229
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,530
Pause and try it.

230
00:13:40,390 --> 00:13:42,120
One way is to factor.

231
00:13:42,310 --> 00:13:49,290
Two x squared minus seven x minus fifteen
factors into the quantity two x plus

232
00:13:49,310 --> 00:13:52,810
three, times the quantity x minus five.

233
00:13:52,830 --> 00:13:56,800
So the solutions are negative
three halves and five.

234
00:13:57,340 --> 00:13:58,320
Add them.

235
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:01,079
Five minus one and a
half is three and a half.

236
00:14:01,099 --> 00:14:05,110
So the answer is three
point five, or seven halves.

237
00:14:05,339 --> 00:14:08,510
Either form works in the answer box.

238
00:14:08,969 --> 00:14:10,339
There's also a shortcut.

239
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:15,939
For any quadratic, a x
squared plus b x plus c,

240
00:14:16,329 --> 00:14:19,819
the solutions add up to negative b over a.

241
00:14:19,889 --> 00:14:22,188
Here that's seven over two.

242
00:14:22,208 --> 00:14:24,378
Same answer, no factoring.

243
00:14:24,805 --> 00:14:26,615
Or use Desmos.

244
00:14:26,764 --> 00:14:31,665
Graph y equals two x squared
minus seven x minus fifteen,

245
00:14:31,685 --> 00:14:33,344
and click the curve.

246
00:14:33,364 --> 00:14:38,184
The x intercepts show up at
negative one point five and five.

247
00:14:38,204 --> 00:14:39,204
Add them.

248
00:14:39,548 --> 00:14:40,918
Question eleven.

249
00:14:41,068 --> 00:14:46,398
An elevator has a maximum capacity
of one thousand five hundred pounds.

250
00:14:46,588 --> 00:14:51,328
A worker who weighs one hundred eighty
pounds will ride in the elevator with b

251
00:14:51,348 --> 00:14:55,037
boxes that each weigh forty-five pounds.

252
00:14:55,058 --> 00:15:00,758
Which inequality represents all possible
values of b for one trip without

253
00:15:00,778 --> 00:15:02,388
exceeding the capacity?

254
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:04,160
Pause and try it.

255
00:15:10,020 --> 00:15:12,480
Build the total weight piece by piece.

256
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:14,440
The worker is one hundred eighty pounds,

257
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:15,360
once.

258
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:18,920
Each box is forty-five
pounds, and there are b boxes,

259
00:15:18,940 --> 00:15:20,800
so that's forty-five b.

260
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:24,509
The total weight is one hundred
eighty plus forty-five b.

261
00:15:24,945 --> 00:15:29,845
Maximum capacity means the total can't
go over one thousand five hundred.

262
00:15:29,865 --> 00:15:31,765
It can equal it, or be less.

263
00:15:31,785 --> 00:15:33,484
That's less than or equal to.

264
00:15:33,504 --> 00:15:37,805
So one hundred eighty plus forty-five
b is less than or equal to one thousand

265
00:15:37,825 --> 00:15:38,685
five hundred.

266
00:15:38,705 --> 00:15:40,075
The answer is B.

267
00:15:40,542 --> 00:15:42,522
A swaps the two weights.

268
00:15:42,542 --> 00:15:46,522
C flips the sign, which would mean
the elevator has to be overloaded.

269
00:15:46,542 --> 00:15:50,442
And D adds the worker's
weight to the capacity,

270
00:15:50,462 --> 00:15:53,351
as if the worker made
the elevator stronger.

271
00:15:53,809 --> 00:15:58,149
A common follow-up asks for
the greatest number of boxes.

272
00:15:58,169 --> 00:16:02,669
Subtract one hundred eighty, and
forty-five b is at most one thousand three

273
00:16:02,689 --> 00:16:04,058
hundred twenty.

274
00:16:04,089 --> 00:16:08,369
Divide, and b is at most
about twenty-nine point three.

275
00:16:08,389 --> 00:16:13,089
You can't take part of a box, and
rounding up would overload the elevator,

276
00:16:13,109 --> 00:16:15,159
so the answer would be twenty-nine.

277
00:16:15,714 --> 00:16:16,934
Question twelve.

278
00:16:16,954 --> 00:16:23,693
The value V, in dollars, of a car t years
after it was purchased is modeled by V

279
00:16:23,713 --> 00:16:29,244
of t equals twenty-four thousand
times zero point eight five to the t.

280
00:16:29,514 --> 00:16:34,134
Which statement best describes how the
value of the car changes each year,

281
00:16:34,154 --> 00:16:35,524
according to the model?

282
00:16:35,962 --> 00:16:37,252
Pause and try it.

283
00:16:43,112 --> 00:16:49,042
In an exponential model, the number being
raised to the t is the growth factor.

284
00:16:49,192 --> 00:16:54,282
Each year, the value gets
multiplied by zero point eight five.

285
00:16:54,431 --> 00:16:58,091
Multiplying by zero point eight
five keeps eighty-five percent,

286
00:16:58,111 --> 00:17:00,332
which means you lose fifteen percent.

287
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:02,482
The answer is D.

288
00:17:02,929 --> 00:17:04,509
B is the most common trap.

289
00:17:04,529 --> 00:17:07,869
Eighty-five percent is
what's left, not what's lost.

290
00:17:07,889 --> 00:17:13,068
A car that lost eighty-five percent every
year would be worth just five hundred

291
00:17:13,088 --> 00:17:15,699
forty dollars after two years.

292
00:17:16,140 --> 00:17:17,720
C is sneakier.

293
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:22,080
Fifteen percent of twenty-four
thousand is three thousand six hundred,

294
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:24,519
so the car does lose that
much in the first year.

295
00:17:24,539 --> 00:17:28,240
But the next year it loses fifteen
percent of a smaller value,

296
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:30,320
so the dollar amount shrinks.

297
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,680
A constant dollar drop would be linear,

298
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:34,110
not exponential.

299
00:17:34,599 --> 00:17:37,208
Here's a quick way to
read any growth factor.

300
00:17:39,119 --> 00:17:40,649
Subtract one.

301
00:17:40,799 --> 00:17:45,898
Zero point eight five minus one
is negative zero point one five,

302
00:17:45,918 --> 00:17:48,209
a fifteen percent decrease.

303
00:17:48,279 --> 00:17:52,689
A factor of one point zero four
would mean a four percent increase.

304
00:17:53,083 --> 00:17:54,383
Question thirteen.

305
00:17:54,403 --> 00:17:57,943
In right triangle P Q R,
angle R is a right angle.

306
00:17:57,963 --> 00:18:02,023
The length of hypotenuse
P Q is twenty-six,

307
00:18:02,043 --> 00:18:05,663
and cosine of P equals five thirteenths.

308
00:18:05,683 --> 00:18:07,652
What is the length of Q R?

309
00:18:08,067 --> 00:18:09,357
Pause and try it.

310
00:18:15,217 --> 00:18:18,346
Draw it, with the right angle at R.

311
00:18:18,377 --> 00:18:21,787
Cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse.

312
00:18:22,257 --> 00:18:26,827
From angle P, the adjacent side is P R.

313
00:18:26,856 --> 00:18:31,427
So P R over twenty-six
equals five thirteenths,

314
00:18:31,537 --> 00:18:33,907
and P R is ten.

315
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:35,793
Q R is the other leg.

316
00:18:35,813 --> 00:18:37,833
Use the Pythagorean theorem.

317
00:18:37,853 --> 00:18:42,513
Ten squared plus Q R squared
equals twenty-six squared.

318
00:18:42,533 --> 00:18:47,783
That's one hundred plus Q R squared
equals six hundred seventy-six.

319
00:18:47,812 --> 00:18:51,033
So Q R squared is five
hundred seventy-six,

320
00:18:51,053 --> 00:18:53,263
and Q R is twenty-four.

321
00:18:53,373 --> 00:18:55,063
The answer is C.

322
00:18:55,525 --> 00:19:00,705
Faster: five, twelve, thirteen
is a Pythagorean triple,

323
00:19:00,725 --> 00:19:03,695
and this triangle is that one doubled.

324
00:19:03,805 --> 00:19:06,895
Ten, twenty-four, twenty-six.

325
00:19:07,164 --> 00:19:10,545
Ten is P R, the trap if you stop early.

326
00:19:10,565 --> 00:19:12,465
Twelve forgets to double.

327
00:19:12,485 --> 00:19:17,215
And twenty-six can't be a leg, because
legs are shorter than the hypotenuse.

328
00:19:17,725 --> 00:19:19,095
Question fourteen.

329
00:19:19,405 --> 00:19:24,745
For the linear function g, the table
shows three values of x and their

330
00:19:24,765 --> 00:19:27,255
corresponding values of g of x.

331
00:19:27,364 --> 00:19:30,815
When x is negative one, g of x is eleven.

332
00:19:30,884 --> 00:19:33,865
When x is two, g of x is two.

333
00:19:33,885 --> 00:19:37,295
When x is five, g of x is negative seven.

334
00:19:37,605 --> 00:19:39,575
Which equation defines g?

335
00:19:40,185 --> 00:19:41,475
Pause and try it.

336
00:19:47,335 --> 00:19:50,194
Find the slope from any two rows.

337
00:19:50,214 --> 00:19:53,355
From x equals negative
one to x equals two,

338
00:19:53,375 --> 00:19:58,235
x goes up three, and g of x
goes from eleven down to two,

339
00:19:58,255 --> 00:19:59,824
a drop of nine.

340
00:20:00,055 --> 00:20:03,105
Negative nine over
three is negative three.

341
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:05,130
Now find the intercept.

342
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:07,770
Use the row where x is two.

343
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:11,290
Two equals negative
three times two, plus b.

344
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:13,859
That's two equals negative six plus b,

345
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,380
so b is eight.

346
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:19,500
The function is g of x equals
negative three x plus eight.

347
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,570
The answer is A.

348
00:20:22,023 --> 00:20:23,203
Here's the trap.

349
00:20:23,223 --> 00:20:26,123
C and D both work for the first row.

350
00:20:26,143 --> 00:20:29,553
Plug in negative one, and
each one gives eleven.

351
00:20:29,623 --> 00:20:31,562
But neither works for the second row.

352
00:20:31,582 --> 00:20:36,553
A table question isn't done until
your equation fits every row.

353
00:20:36,997 --> 00:20:38,617
Desmos can do this too.

354
00:20:38,637 --> 00:20:43,817
Add a table, and enter the three
points in the x one and y one columns.

355
00:20:43,837 --> 00:20:48,607
Then type y one, tilde, m x one plus b.

356
00:20:48,757 --> 00:20:53,927
Desmos reports m equals negative
three and b equals eight.

357
00:20:54,367 --> 00:20:55,707
Question fifteen.

358
00:20:55,727 --> 00:21:01,867
The function f is defined by f of
x equals x squared minus ten x plus

359
00:21:01,887 --> 00:21:02,887
twenty-one.

360
00:21:03,366 --> 00:21:07,147
Which of the following is an equivalent
form of the function that displays the

361
00:21:07,167 --> 00:21:11,017
minimum value of f as a
constant or coefficient?

362
00:21:11,542 --> 00:21:12,832
Pause and try it.

363
00:21:18,692 --> 00:21:23,062
The minimum of a parabola is
the y value of its vertex.

364
00:21:23,092 --> 00:21:26,432
The form that shows the
vertex is vertex form:

365
00:21:26,452 --> 00:21:31,472
a times the quantity x minus h, squared,

366
00:21:31,492 --> 00:21:32,702
plus k.

367
00:21:33,052 --> 00:21:37,752
The vertex is h, k, and
when the parabola opens up,

368
00:21:37,772 --> 00:21:39,462
k is the minimum.

369
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:41,430
Complete the square.

370
00:21:41,859 --> 00:21:45,320
Half of negative ten is negative five,

371
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:48,149
and negative five squared is twenty-five.

372
00:21:48,459 --> 00:21:52,750
Add twenty-five and subtract
twenty-five to keep things balanced.

373
00:21:52,770 --> 00:21:56,110
That's the quantity x minus five, squared,

374
00:21:56,130 --> 00:22:00,550
plus twenty-one minus twenty-five,
which is the quantity x minus five,

375
00:22:00,570 --> 00:22:02,420
squared, minus four.

376
00:22:02,839 --> 00:22:07,219
The minimum value is negative four, and
it's sitting right there as a constant.

377
00:22:07,239 --> 00:22:09,459
The answer is A.

378
00:22:09,479 --> 00:22:13,378
B has the wrong sign inside,
so it isn't equivalent.

379
00:22:13,398 --> 00:22:16,499
C and D are equivalent,
but C shows the zeros,

380
00:22:16,519 --> 00:22:20,529
three and seven, and D doesn't
show the minimum at all.

381
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,460
If completing the square is slow for you,

382
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:25,570
find the vertex directly.

383
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:29,539
The x coordinate is negative b over two a,

384
00:22:29,559 --> 00:22:32,260
which is ten over two, or five.

385
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:36,459
Then f of five is twenty-five
minus fifty plus twenty-one,

386
00:22:36,479 --> 00:22:37,980
which is negative four.

387
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:39,530
Same minimum.

388
00:22:39,951 --> 00:22:46,241
Desmos check: graph y equals x
squared minus ten x plus twenty-one,

389
00:22:46,271 --> 00:22:48,211
and click the bottom of the curve.

390
00:22:48,231 --> 00:22:51,280
The vertex is five, negative four.

391
00:22:51,430 --> 00:22:54,760
Then pick the choice
that shows negative four.

392
00:22:55,225 --> 00:22:56,965
Another pacing check.

393
00:22:56,985 --> 00:23:00,275
At an even ninety-five
seconds per question,

394
00:23:00,385 --> 00:23:04,325
you'd start question sixteen at
about the twenty-four minute mark.

395
00:23:04,345 --> 00:23:06,645
If you got here sooner, good.

396
00:23:06,665 --> 00:23:11,315
That extra time is exactly what
the last seven questions need.

397
00:23:11,808 --> 00:23:13,378
Question sixteen.

398
00:23:14,008 --> 00:23:16,298
This is where the module gets hard.

399
00:23:16,528 --> 00:23:21,148
In the equation five times
the quantity x minus two k,

400
00:23:21,168 --> 00:23:24,308
plus three x, equals a x plus twenty,

401
00:23:24,328 --> 00:23:26,537
a and k are constants.

402
00:23:26,768 --> 00:23:29,988
If the equation has
infinitely many solutions,

403
00:23:30,008 --> 00:23:32,898
what is the value of a plus k?

404
00:23:33,349 --> 00:23:34,639
Pause and try it.

405
00:23:41,499 --> 00:23:46,359
A linear equation has infinitely many
solutions when both sides are exactly the

406
00:23:46,379 --> 00:23:47,869
same expression.

407
00:23:48,139 --> 00:23:50,509
So simplify the left side first.

408
00:23:50,738 --> 00:23:57,269
Five times the quantity x minus
two k is five x minus ten k.

409
00:23:57,779 --> 00:24:03,389
Add three x, and the left
side is eight x minus ten k.

410
00:24:03,882 --> 00:24:06,422
Now match the two sides piece by piece.

411
00:24:06,442 --> 00:24:10,212
The x terms must match, so a equals eight.

412
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:14,142
The constants must match, so
negative ten k equals twenty,

413
00:24:14,162 --> 00:24:16,492
and k equals negative two.

414
00:24:17,032 --> 00:24:21,332
So a plus k is eight plus negative two,

415
00:24:21,352 --> 00:24:22,762
which is six.

416
00:24:22,832 --> 00:24:24,122
Type six.

417
00:24:24,528 --> 00:24:25,388
Two traps here.

418
00:24:25,408 --> 00:24:28,427
If you forget the three
x, you'll think a is five.

419
00:24:28,447 --> 00:24:31,268
And if you drop the negative sign on k,

420
00:24:31,288 --> 00:24:34,378
you'll end up with ten instead of six.

421
00:24:34,687 --> 00:24:39,948
Remember the rule: same x coefficient
and same constant means infinitely many

422
00:24:39,968 --> 00:24:40,948
solutions.

423
00:24:40,968 --> 00:24:45,498
Same x coefficient but a different
constant means no solution.

424
00:24:45,952 --> 00:24:47,562
Question seventeen.

425
00:24:48,912 --> 00:24:53,482
A data set consists of seven
different positive integers.

426
00:24:53,592 --> 00:24:58,761
The mean of the data set is
ten, and the median is nine.

427
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:04,162
What is the greatest possible value of
the largest integer in the data set?

428
00:25:04,689 --> 00:25:05,979
Pause and try it.

429
00:25:12,839 --> 00:25:14,739
Turn the mean into a total.

430
00:25:14,759 --> 00:25:18,449
Seven numbers with a mean
of ten add up to seventy.

431
00:25:18,519 --> 00:25:22,218
And the median of seven numbers
is the fourth one in order.

432
00:25:22,238 --> 00:25:24,568
So the middle slot is nine.

433
00:25:25,012 --> 00:25:27,871
To make the largest
number as big as possible,

434
00:25:27,891 --> 00:25:31,632
make every other number
as small as possible.

435
00:25:31,652 --> 00:25:36,032
The three numbers below nine have
to be different positive integers,

436
00:25:36,052 --> 00:25:39,832
so the smallest they can be is one, two,

437
00:25:39,852 --> 00:25:40,852
and three.

438
00:25:41,232 --> 00:25:45,332
The two numbers right after nine have to
be bigger than nine and different from

439
00:25:45,352 --> 00:25:49,242
each other, so the smallest
options are ten and eleven.

440
00:25:49,391 --> 00:25:52,721
Now add up everything
except the last slot.

441
00:25:52,791 --> 00:25:59,242
One plus two plus three plus nine
plus ten plus eleven is thirty-six.

442
00:25:59,810 --> 00:26:04,590
The total has to be seventy, so the
last number is seventy minus thirty-six,

443
00:26:04,610 --> 00:26:06,020
which is thirty-four.

444
00:26:06,370 --> 00:26:07,740
Type thirty-four.

445
00:26:08,209 --> 00:26:10,500
Quick check: the numbers
are all different,

446
00:26:10,530 --> 00:26:14,180
the median is nine, and
the total is seventy.

447
00:26:14,645 --> 00:26:17,585
The common mistake is
ignoring the word different.

448
00:26:17,605 --> 00:26:20,985
If repeats were allowed,
you could use one,

449
00:26:21,005 --> 00:26:25,944
one, one, and nine, nine,
nine, and get forty.

450
00:26:25,964 --> 00:26:28,054
That's the answer to a different question.

451
00:26:28,532 --> 00:26:30,032
Question eighteen.

452
00:26:30,052 --> 00:26:35,032
What is the solution to the equation
x over the quantity x minus three,

453
00:26:35,052 --> 00:26:40,622
minus two, equals three over
the quantity x minus three?

454
00:26:41,062 --> 00:26:42,352
Pause and try it.

455
00:26:49,212 --> 00:26:51,712
Before anything else,
look at the denominators.

456
00:26:51,732 --> 00:26:55,872
x minus three can't be
zero, so x can't be three.

457
00:26:55,892 --> 00:26:59,101
Write that down now, because
it decides this question.

458
00:26:59,526 --> 00:27:04,136
Now clear the fractions by multiplying
every term by x minus three.

459
00:27:04,246 --> 00:27:08,426
You get x minus two times
the quantity x minus three,

460
00:27:08,446 --> 00:27:10,106
equals three.

461
00:27:10,126 --> 00:27:14,266
Distribute: x minus two
x plus six equals three.

462
00:27:14,286 --> 00:27:17,346
That's negative x plus six equals three,

463
00:27:17,366 --> 00:27:19,096
so x equals three.

464
00:27:19,514 --> 00:27:24,134
But x equals three makes
the denominators zero.

465
00:27:24,154 --> 00:27:27,204
It's an extraneous solution,
so it doesn't count.

466
00:27:27,234 --> 00:27:31,334
Nothing else is left, which means
the equation has no solution.

467
00:27:31,354 --> 00:27:33,083
The answer is D.

468
00:27:33,507 --> 00:27:35,757
Desmos makes this visual.

469
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:40,527
Graph the left side as one function
and the right side as another.

470
00:27:40,547 --> 00:27:44,367
The left side is the right
side shifted down by one,

471
00:27:44,387 --> 00:27:46,566
so the two curves never cross.

472
00:27:46,586 --> 00:27:49,277
No intersection, no solution.

473
00:27:49,708 --> 00:27:52,047
A and B are just numbers that don't check.

474
00:27:52,067 --> 00:27:53,248
Try zero.

475
00:27:53,268 --> 00:27:57,248
The left side is negative two, and
the right side is negative one.

476
00:27:57,268 --> 00:27:58,437
Not equal.

477
00:27:58,548 --> 00:28:02,478
On rational equations, always
check your answer in the original.

478
00:28:02,939 --> 00:28:04,389
Question nineteen.

479
00:28:04,459 --> 00:28:08,519
The graph of y equals f of x
passes through the point two,

480
00:28:08,539 --> 00:28:09,589
five.

481
00:28:09,819 --> 00:28:16,398
The function g is defined by g of x
equals f of the quantity x plus four,

482
00:28:16,418 --> 00:28:17,879
minus three.

483
00:28:17,899 --> 00:28:22,349
Which point must lie on the
graph of y equals g of x?

484
00:28:22,806 --> 00:28:24,096
Pause and try it.

485
00:28:30,956 --> 00:28:32,246
There are two changes.

486
00:28:32,276 --> 00:28:34,976
The minus three is outside the function,

487
00:28:34,996 --> 00:28:37,576
so it moves the graph down three.

488
00:28:37,596 --> 00:28:39,365
That one does what it looks like.

489
00:28:39,396 --> 00:28:44,456
The plus four is inside, next to x,
and inside changes work backwards.

490
00:28:44,476 --> 00:28:47,136
Plus four shifts the graph left four,

491
00:28:47,156 --> 00:28:48,156
not right.

492
00:28:48,532 --> 00:28:52,391
So move the point two, five
left four and down three.

493
00:28:52,411 --> 00:28:54,512
Two minus four is negative two.

494
00:28:54,532 --> 00:28:56,511
Five minus three is two.

495
00:28:56,531 --> 00:28:59,392
The new point is negative two, two.

496
00:28:59,412 --> 00:29:01,101
The answer is B.

497
00:29:01,543 --> 00:29:03,563
You can also confirm it directly.

498
00:29:03,583 --> 00:29:06,403
Plug in x equals negative two.

499
00:29:06,423 --> 00:29:10,842
g of negative two is f of
negative two plus four,

500
00:29:10,862 --> 00:29:12,002
minus three.

501
00:29:12,022 --> 00:29:14,602
That's f of two, minus three.

502
00:29:14,622 --> 00:29:18,923
f of two is five, so g
of negative two is two.

503
00:29:18,943 --> 00:29:20,073
It checks.

504
00:29:20,566 --> 00:29:25,976
Choice A is the classic mistake:
shifting right instead of left.

505
00:29:26,006 --> 00:29:30,226
C shifts left, but up
three instead of down.

506
00:29:30,246 --> 00:29:32,975
And D makes both mistakes.

507
00:29:33,447 --> 00:29:34,547
Question twenty.

508
00:29:34,567 --> 00:29:37,297
Here's a system of inequalities.

509
00:29:37,647 --> 00:29:43,057
y is less than or equal to
negative two x plus ten,

510
00:29:43,086 --> 00:29:46,417
and y is greater than x plus one.

511
00:29:46,487 --> 00:29:50,307
If the point a, b is a
solution to the system,

512
00:29:50,327 --> 00:29:54,057
what is the greatest
possible integer value of a?

513
00:29:54,524 --> 00:29:55,814
Pause and try it.

514
00:30:02,674 --> 00:30:05,134
a is the x coordinate of the point.

515
00:30:05,154 --> 00:30:09,294
For a point to work, y has
to be above x plus one,

516
00:30:09,314 --> 00:30:13,444
and at or below negative two x plus ten.

517
00:30:13,474 --> 00:30:19,284
That's only possible where x plus one
is less than negative two x plus ten.

518
00:30:19,756 --> 00:30:20,616
Solve that.

519
00:30:20,636 --> 00:30:26,606
Add two x to both sides, and
three x plus one is less than ten.

520
00:30:26,716 --> 00:30:30,895
Then three x is less than
nine, so x is less than three.

521
00:30:30,915 --> 00:30:33,975
The greatest integer
less than three is two.

522
00:30:33,995 --> 00:30:35,846
The answer is A.

523
00:30:36,267 --> 00:30:38,597
Desmos shows why.

524
00:30:38,747 --> 00:30:41,437
Graph both inequalities.

525
00:30:41,507 --> 00:30:46,646
The overlap is a wedge that narrows to
a point where the boundary lines cross.

526
00:30:46,666 --> 00:30:51,646
To find that point exactly, type the two
lines as plain equations and click the

527
00:30:51,666 --> 00:30:52,527
intersection.

528
00:30:52,547 --> 00:30:54,677
It's three, four.

529
00:30:55,133 --> 00:30:58,113
But the line y equals
x plus one is dashed,

530
00:30:58,133 --> 00:31:00,953
because the inequality
is strictly greater than.

531
00:31:00,973 --> 00:31:06,153
So the corner point isn't included, and
no point with x equal to three works.

532
00:31:06,173 --> 00:31:07,953
That's why three is the trap.

533
00:31:07,973 --> 00:31:13,073
Four is the y value of the corner, and
five is where the solid line crosses the

534
00:31:13,093 --> 00:31:14,143
x axis.

535
00:31:14,613 --> 00:31:16,473
And you can confirm that two works.

536
00:31:16,493 --> 00:31:21,553
With a equal to two, y has to be
greater than three and at most six.

537
00:31:21,573 --> 00:31:24,152
So the point two, four is a solution.

538
00:31:24,172 --> 00:31:27,353
Plug it in: four is less
than or equal to six,

539
00:31:27,373 --> 00:31:29,553
and four is greater than three.

540
00:31:29,573 --> 00:31:30,703
Both are true.

541
00:31:31,112 --> 00:31:31,932
Question twenty-one.

542
00:31:31,952 --> 00:31:36,252
In the x y plane, the graph
of the quantity x minus three,

543
00:31:36,272 --> 00:31:38,852
squared, plus the quantity y plus one,

544
00:31:38,872 --> 00:31:43,402
squared, equals twenty-five is a circle.

545
00:31:43,591 --> 00:31:47,012
Line L is tangent to the
circle at the point six,

546
00:31:47,032 --> 00:31:47,852
three.

547
00:31:47,872 --> 00:31:50,202
What is the slope of line L?

548
00:31:50,646 --> 00:31:51,936
Pause and try it.

549
00:31:59,796 --> 00:32:02,126
Read the center from the equation.

550
00:32:02,476 --> 00:32:07,286
The quantity x minus three
means the x coordinate is three.

551
00:32:07,396 --> 00:32:12,086
The quantity y plus one means
the y coordinate is negative one.

552
00:32:12,195 --> 00:32:15,496
So the center is three, negative one,

553
00:32:15,516 --> 00:32:17,406
and the radius is five.

554
00:32:17,946 --> 00:32:19,316
Here's the key fact.

555
00:32:19,346 --> 00:32:24,716
A tangent line is perpendicular to the
radius at the point where it touches.

556
00:32:24,786 --> 00:32:28,405
So find the slope of the
radius, from the center,

557
00:32:28,425 --> 00:32:31,366
three, negative one, to the point six,

558
00:32:31,386 --> 00:32:32,245
three.

559
00:32:32,265 --> 00:32:34,806
The rise is three minus negative one,

560
00:32:34,826 --> 00:32:36,006
which is four.

561
00:32:36,026 --> 00:32:39,116
The run is six minus
three, which is three.

562
00:32:39,136 --> 00:32:42,225
The radius has slope four thirds.

563
00:32:42,746 --> 00:32:45,806
Perpendicular slopes are
negative reciprocals.

564
00:32:45,826 --> 00:32:48,766
Flip four thirds and change the sign,

565
00:32:48,786 --> 00:32:51,166
and you get negative three fourths.

566
00:32:51,186 --> 00:32:53,036
The answer is B.

567
00:32:53,498 --> 00:32:56,638
D, four thirds, is the
slope of the radius,

568
00:32:56,658 --> 00:32:59,508
and it's the most tempting wrong answer.

569
00:32:59,538 --> 00:33:03,708
A and C each do only half
of the negative reciprocal.

570
00:33:03,817 --> 00:33:09,508
A changes the sign without flipping,
and C flips without changing the sign.

571
00:33:10,006 --> 00:33:13,336
Desmos check: type the circle equation,

572
00:33:13,566 --> 00:33:19,985
then the line y minus three equals
negative three fourths times the quantity x

573
00:33:20,005 --> 00:33:21,495
minus six.

574
00:33:21,726 --> 00:33:23,786
Press the right arrow after the four,

575
00:33:23,806 --> 00:33:26,936
so the parentheses don't
end up in the denominator.

576
00:33:27,006 --> 00:33:30,426
The line touches the circle
at exactly one point,

577
00:33:30,446 --> 00:33:31,706
six, three.

578
00:33:31,726 --> 00:33:36,696
Try the slope four thirds instead, and
the line cuts right through the center.

579
00:33:37,110 --> 00:33:39,440
Last question, and the hardest.

580
00:33:39,590 --> 00:33:44,130
The equation x squared minus
eight x plus c equals zero,

581
00:33:44,150 --> 00:33:47,089
where c is a constant,
has two real solutions.

582
00:33:47,109 --> 00:33:49,690
One solution is three times the other.

583
00:33:49,710 --> 00:33:51,679
What is the value of c?

584
00:33:52,134 --> 00:33:53,354
Pause and try it.

585
00:33:53,374 --> 00:33:55,143
Take a little longer on this one.

586
00:34:03,921 --> 00:34:05,301
Give the solutions names.

587
00:34:05,321 --> 00:34:06,901
Call one solution r.

588
00:34:06,921 --> 00:34:09,421
Then the other one is three r.

589
00:34:09,441 --> 00:34:15,570
If those are the solutions, the quadratic
factors as the quantity x minus r,

590
00:34:15,641 --> 00:34:18,451
times the quantity x minus three r.

591
00:34:18,867 --> 00:34:24,887
Expand that, and you get x squared
minus four r x plus three r squared.

592
00:34:24,907 --> 00:34:29,997
Now match it to x squared
minus eight x plus c.

593
00:34:30,667 --> 00:34:34,567
The x terms must match,
so four r equals eight,

594
00:34:34,587 --> 00:34:36,557
and r equals two.

595
00:34:36,961 --> 00:34:39,811
So the solutions are two and six.

596
00:34:39,961 --> 00:34:42,571
The constant term c is three r squared,

597
00:34:43,321 --> 00:34:46,571
which is three times four, or twelve.

598
00:34:47,241 --> 00:34:48,530
Type twelve.

599
00:34:49,030 --> 00:34:49,930
Check it.

600
00:34:49,950 --> 00:34:57,049
x squared minus eight x plus twelve
factors into the quantity x minus two,

601
00:34:57,069 --> 00:35:00,120
times the quantity x minus six.

602
00:35:00,230 --> 00:35:05,010
The solutions are two and six,
and six is three times two.

603
00:35:05,030 --> 00:35:06,080
It works.

604
00:35:06,544 --> 00:35:08,324
There's a shortcut if you know it.

605
00:35:08,344 --> 00:35:13,444
The solutions of x squared minus
eight x plus c add up to eight.

606
00:35:13,464 --> 00:35:18,444
So r plus three r equals
eight, and r is two.

607
00:35:18,464 --> 00:35:20,603
Then c is the product of the solutions,

608
00:35:20,623 --> 00:35:22,914
two times six, which is twelve.

609
00:35:23,405 --> 00:35:24,945
One trap to avoid.

610
00:35:24,965 --> 00:35:30,065
Some students set the discriminant
equal to zero and get c equals sixteen.

611
00:35:30,085 --> 00:35:33,944
But that makes x squared
minus eight x plus sixteen,

612
00:35:33,964 --> 00:35:36,745
which has only one solution, four.

613
00:35:36,765 --> 00:35:38,985
The question says two real solutions,

614
00:35:39,005 --> 00:35:41,015
so sixteen can't work.

615
00:35:41,508 --> 00:35:43,968
And in Desmos, once you have an answer,

616
00:35:43,988 --> 00:35:48,208
graph y equals x squared
minus eight x plus twelve,

617
00:35:48,228 --> 00:35:50,647
and click the x intercepts.

618
00:35:50,667 --> 00:35:52,127
Two and six.

619
00:35:52,147 --> 00:35:54,237
One is three times the other.

620
00:35:54,699 --> 00:35:55,909
That's all twenty-two.

621
00:35:56,419 --> 00:35:58,188
Count how many you got right.

622
00:35:58,259 --> 00:36:02,469
Then do something more useful:
sort your misses by domain.

623
00:36:02,930 --> 00:36:06,669
Algebra was questions one, four, seven,

624
00:36:06,689 --> 00:36:10,830
eight, eleven, fourteen,
sixteen, and twenty.

625
00:36:10,850 --> 00:36:13,389
That's eight questions
on linear equations,

626
00:36:13,409 --> 00:36:16,739
linear functions,
systems, and inequalities.

627
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:19,979
Advanced math was questions three, six,

628
00:36:19,999 --> 00:36:23,860
ten, twelve, fifteen, eighteen, nineteen,

629
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:24,970
and twenty-two.

630
00:36:25,239 --> 00:36:29,020
Also eight questions:
quadratics, functions,

631
00:36:29,040 --> 00:36:32,410
an exponential model,
and a rational equation.

632
00:36:32,850 --> 00:36:36,069
Problem solving and data
analysis was questions two,

633
00:36:36,089 --> 00:36:37,870
nine, and seventeen.

634
00:36:37,890 --> 00:36:40,630
Geometry and trigonometry
was questions five,

635
00:36:40,650 --> 00:36:42,579
thirteen, and twenty-one.

636
00:36:42,690 --> 00:36:46,590
That split, eight,
eight, three, and three,

637
00:36:46,610 --> 00:36:51,060
roughly matches how the real
test weights the four domains.

638
00:36:51,543 --> 00:36:55,123
Now, don't turn your
count into an SAT score.

639
00:36:55,143 --> 00:37:00,162
On the real test, two students with the
same number correct can get different

640
00:37:00,182 --> 00:37:04,323
scores, because scoring looks at
which questions you got right,

641
00:37:04,343 --> 00:37:06,162
including how hard they were.

642
00:37:06,182 --> 00:37:11,723
And each module includes two unscored
pretest questions that you can't tell

643
00:37:11,743 --> 00:37:13,113
apart from the rest.

644
00:37:13,578 --> 00:37:15,998
So use your misses to find patterns.

645
00:37:16,018 --> 00:37:17,477
Start with where they happened.

646
00:37:17,497 --> 00:37:20,358
Questions one through
seven were the easiest.

647
00:37:20,378 --> 00:37:23,918
A miss there is usually a slip, not a gap:

648
00:37:23,938 --> 00:37:27,358
a sign error, or answering a
different question than the one asked.

649
00:37:27,378 --> 00:37:31,308
The fix is a ten second
reread before you lock in.

650
00:37:31,782 --> 00:37:35,072
Questions eight through
fifteen were the core skills:

651
00:37:35,101 --> 00:37:39,482
systems, probability,
quadratics, exponential models,

652
00:37:39,502 --> 00:37:40,671
and trig.

653
00:37:40,902 --> 00:37:43,882
A miss there points to a skill to review.

654
00:37:43,902 --> 00:37:46,872
Write down the skill, not
just the question number.

655
00:37:47,326 --> 00:37:50,746
Questions sixteen through
twenty-two were the hard tier.

656
00:37:50,766 --> 00:37:53,706
If you ran out of time
before you reached them,

657
00:37:53,726 --> 00:37:56,346
the problem may be pacing, not math.

658
00:37:56,366 --> 00:37:59,616
Check how long the first
fifteen questions took you.

659
00:38:00,017 --> 00:38:02,147
Here's how to sort any miss.

660
00:38:02,177 --> 00:38:05,517
Redo it untimed before
you rewatch the solution.

661
00:38:05,537 --> 00:38:09,837
If you get it right with no clock,
it was time pressure or a slip.

662
00:38:09,857 --> 00:38:12,396
If you still can't do
it, it's a skill gap,

663
00:38:12,416 --> 00:38:14,826
and that skill goes on your study list.

664
00:38:15,267 --> 00:38:17,606
Two pacing habits help most.

665
00:38:17,626 --> 00:38:22,247
First, if a question stalls you,
use the bookmark to flag it,

666
00:38:22,267 --> 00:38:24,246
guess, and come back later.

667
00:38:24,266 --> 00:38:27,367
Second, never leave a question blank.

668
00:38:27,387 --> 00:38:29,767
The College Board says
that for most students,

669
00:38:29,787 --> 00:38:33,037
it's better to guess than
to leave a question blank.

670
00:38:33,567 --> 00:38:34,977
Here's the recap.

671
00:38:35,087 --> 00:38:39,337
A lot of the points in this
module came down to a few habits.

672
00:38:39,447 --> 00:38:43,706
Reread what the question
asks for: angle C,

673
00:38:43,726 --> 00:38:47,747
not angle B, and the sale
price, not the discount.

674
00:38:47,767 --> 00:38:49,827
Put parentheses around negatives.

675
00:38:49,847 --> 00:38:52,537
And in a table, check every row.

676
00:38:53,031 --> 00:38:56,051
On the hard questions, a
few rules did the work.

677
00:38:56,071 --> 00:38:59,931
In probability, the group you're
choosing from is your denominator.

678
00:38:59,951 --> 00:39:02,801
Inside a function, shifts go backwards.

679
00:39:02,831 --> 00:39:05,771
A tangent line is
perpendicular to the radius.

680
00:39:05,791 --> 00:39:08,961
And always check for extraneous solutions.

681
00:39:09,417 --> 00:39:13,677
And use Desmos where it's faster:
intersections for systems,

682
00:39:13,697 --> 00:39:17,516
x intercepts for quadratics,
the vertex for a minimum,

683
00:39:17,536 --> 00:39:19,507
and a regression for a table.

684
00:39:19,983 --> 00:39:25,603
For more practice at any level, the College
Board's free SAT Suite Question Bank

685
00:39:25,623 --> 00:39:29,843
lets you filter by domain,
skill, and difficulty.

686
00:39:29,863 --> 00:39:33,392
Pull questions from your weakest
domain on this scorecard.

687
00:39:33,895 --> 00:39:36,265
If this module helped, subscribe.

688
00:39:36,575 --> 00:39:42,304
Next up is a new set of hard
questions before the March sixth SAT.
